  m_Name: BlastFurnaceData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  engineName: Blast Furnace
  engineDescription: "A Blast Furnace is a large metallurgical furnace used for extracting
    molten iron from iron ore through the process of reduction using coke and limestone.
    Its main components include the furnace stack, hearth, bosh, tuyeres, charging
    system, hot blast stoves, and tapping arrangement. During operation, iron ore,
    coke, and limestone are charged from the top while preheated air is blown through
    the tuyeres, producing high temperatures that reduce iron ore into molten iron
    while removing impurities as slag. \nBlast furnaces are widely used in steel
    manufacturing plants and iron production industries. From an engineering perspective,
    understanding furnace operation, heat transfer, combustion, chemical reactions,
    material flow, energy efficiency, and refractory maintenance is essential for
    achieving high productivity, product quality, and economical iron production."
  engineCategory: Engineering
